      ":question/id": "1529ba15-ecf2-5c3f-871d-ab249ef9af34",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-1125",
      ":question/problem": "Part of the graph of a function $y=f(x)$ with period $2$ is shown below. What is the graph of $y=f(x)$ on the interval $-4\\leq x \\leq 4$?\n\n![](image_assets/ad24b9e538e0ef3e63637e496cfb9032-59abf18dc9.png)",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The graph above shows the function in the interval\n\n$$\n0 \\leq x \\leq 2\n$$\n\nSince this interval has length $2$, and the period of the function is also $2$, this interval represents a single period of the function.\n\nTherefore, the function will consist of many copies of the shape shown above, shifted horizontally by multiples of $2$.\n\n![](image_assets/bbdf4591cae648aba3d16286f3fd7d54-41a583651b.png)"
    },
